# AI code CLI assistants — the landscape (2025–2026)
#
# tools that operate in the terminal, read your codebase, edit files,
# run commands, and handle multi-step coding tasks autonomously.
# distinct from IDE plugins (Copilot in VS Code) or chat UIs (Claude.ai).


# --- major lab CLIs (full agentic) ---

# Claude Code (Anthropic)
# - the benchmark for agentic CLI coding assistants
# - full codebase context, file editing, shell execution, multi-step tasks
# - powered by Claude (Sonnet / Opus)
# - https://claude.ai/code

# Codex CLI (OpenAI)
# - released April 2025; similar agentic approach to Claude Code
# - powered by o3 / o4-mini
# - https://github.com/openai/codex

# Gemini CLI (Google)
# - released June 2025
# - powered by Gemini 2.5 Pro
# - generous free tier at launch
# - https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli


# --- github / microsoft ---

# GitHub Copilot CLI  (gh copilot)
# - lighter weight than the agentic tools above
# - focused on: explain this command, suggest a shell command
# - not a full agentic coding assistant
# - requires GitHub Copilot subscription
# - gh extension install github/gh-copilot


# --- aws ---

# Amazon Q Developer CLI
# - AWS-flavored; strongest for AWS-specific work
#   (CloudFormation, CDK, Lambda, IAM)
# - formerly part of the CodeWhisperer lineage
# - https://aws.amazon.com/q/developer/


# --- open source / model-agnostic ---

# Aider
# - most popular open-source CLI coding assistant
# - model-agnostic: works with Claude, GPT-4, Gemini, local models (Ollama)
# - git-native: commits as it edits, strong for multi-file changes
# - good choice if you want model flexibility or self-hosting
# - pip install aider-chat
# - https://aider.chat

# Goose (Block / Square)
# - open-source agent CLI
# - extensible via plugins / toolkits
# - https://github.com/block/goose


# --- implementation languages ---
#
# Claude Code (Anthropic)   TypeScript / Node.js
# Codex CLI (OpenAI)        Rust  (rewrote from TypeScript; now ~96% Rust, codex-rs)
# Gemini CLI (Google)       TypeScript / Node.js
# GitHub Copilot CLI        Go  (part of the gh CLI ecosystem)
# Amazon Q Developer CLI    Rust
# Aider                     Python  (ML ecosystem is Python-native)
# Goose (Block)             Rust + TypeScript  (primarily Rust; donated to Linux Foundation 2026)
#
# note: Google launched a separate closed-source Go-based Antigravity CLI in
# Jun 2026; Gemini CLI remains open-source on GitHub under Apache 2.0.
#
# Rust is winning for performance-focused rewrites (Codex) and new entrants
# (Amazon Q, Goose) — single static binary, fast startup, no runtime dep.
# TypeScript still dominates where iteration speed and npm ecosystem matter.


# --- how they differ ---

# full agentic (read / edit / run / multi-step):
#   Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Goose, Aider

# command explanation / suggestion (lighter weight, not agentic):
#   GitHub Copilot CLI

# aws-ecosystem specialist:
#   Amazon Q Developer CLI

# model-flexible / self-hostable:
#   Aider (pairs well with Ollama for local models)
